cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite both the paper and the Zenodo deposit."
type: software
title: "QO+R: Analysis code and data for 'A non-monotonic environmental trend in Baryonic Tully-Fisher residuals'"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data tables for Slama (2026), "A non-monotonic
  environmental trend in Baryonic Tully-Fisher residuals: empirical evidence
  and a two-field phenomenological interpretation", Scientific Reports
  (accepted). Includes the BTFR residual analysis (SPARC, ALFALFA), the
  environmental sensitivity tests, the statistical robustness suite, and the
  stratified and multivariate IllustrisTNG analyses. The work is a
  phenomenological consistency test; it does not constitute a quantitative
  test of the two-field framework.
